TGFiZWwxMTkzMjA3MzU4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels/team-Remote-Exec","name":"team-Remote-Exec","color":"f1f442","default":false,"description":"Issues and PRs for the Execution (Remote) team"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2020-07-23T10:24:55Z","updated_at":"2020-08-10T09:25:03Z","closed_at":"2020-08-10T09:25:03Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"> ATTENTION! Please read and follow:\r\n> - if this is a _question_ about how to build / test / query / deploy using Bazel, or a _discussion starter_, send it to bazel-discuss@googlegroups.com\r\n> - if this is a _bug_ or _feature request_, fill the form below as best as you can.\r\n\r\n### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\n`bazel` crashes with `java.lang.IllegalStateException` when `--remote_download_toplevel` is passed to a local build. Often we run remote builds and local builds via a wrapper and keep the same arguments. If the build is not remote (i.e. no --remote_executor) is provided, bazel crashes. \r\n\r\n### Feature requests: what underlying problem are you trying to solve with this feature?\r\n\r\nConsistent behaviour with incompatible flags. If the flag is not compatible, we should errorout. Ideally this flag should be a noop for local builds. \r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nworkspace=$(mktemp -d)\r\ncd $workspace/\r\ntouch WORKSPACE BUILD.bazel\r\nbazel build //... --remote_download_toplevel\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nLinux\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\nrelease 3.4.1","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":